// ECMA-376 Part 1 §20.1.10.56 ST_PresetGeometry — `gear6`.
//
// Data-driven definition copied VERBATIM from
// `presetShapeDefinitions.xml`. A six-toothed gear: the 107-entry
// guide chain places each tooth's flank corners on the pitch ellipse
// via `at2`/`mod`/`cos`/`sin` (the ellipse-radius-at-angle correction
// `na = rw·rh/mod(cos,sin)`), evaluated by the Double-precision
// `guide_engine` rather than hand-transcribed. The six `arcTo` root
// fillets all share the `rw × rh` radii; the spec writes `hR` before
// `wR`, mapped here to `PArcTo(wR=rw, hR=rh, …)`.

///|
/// The verbatim `gear6` preset definition (§20.1.10.56).
fn gear6_def() -> PresetGuideDef {
  {
